WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.106
Most of this course is spent reading research papers.

00:00:03.106 --> 00:00:05.447
Here is a method for reading them critically.

00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:08.557
Ask five questions of every paper.

00:00:08.557 --> 00:00:10.331
What is the single main claim?

00:00:10.331 --> 00:00:13.524
What method was used, where, when, and on what sample?

00:00:13.524 --> 00:00:17.841
Which figure or table carries the evidence, and does its arithmetic hold?

00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:20.797
What uncertainty is reported, and what is missing?

00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:25.587
And finally, scope: to which islands and conditions does the result really apply?

00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:30.891
The annotated papers use a colour code that matches these questions.

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:33.055
Yellow marks the authors' argument.

00:00:33.055 --> 00:00:34.353
Green marks evidence.

00:00:34.353 --> 00:00:35.466
Blue marks method.

00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:37.382
Purple marks concepts to learn.

00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:38.990
Red means read critically.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.339
Orange links the paper to other units.

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.400
Some papers cannot be shared openly,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.048
so for those you get a companion guide and a link to the publisher.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.227
After every video there is a short quiz.

00:00:50.227 --> 00:00:53.712
Get into the habit of answering before you look at the feedback.
